1
00:00:01,199 --> 00:00:07,520
In addition to his private motto of, "I will work harder."

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:12,319
By this time, the weather had broken and the spring plowing had begun.

3
00:00:12,319 --> 00:00:17,600
The shed where Snowball had drawn his plans of the windmill had been shut up,

4
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:22,079
and it was assumed that the plans had been rubbed off the floor.

5
00:00:22,079 --> 00:00:26,600
Every Sunday morning at 10:00, the animals assembled in the big barn to

6
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,119
receive their orders for the week.

7
00:00:29,119 --> 00:00:34,600
The skull of old Major, now clean of flesh, had been disinterred from the

8
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:40,199
orchard and set up on a stump at the foot of the flagstaff beside the gun.

9
00:00:40,199 --> 00:00:44,840
After the hoisting of the flag, the animals were required to file past the

10
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:49,159
skull in a reverent manner before entering the barn.

11
00:00:49,159 --> 00:00:54,319
Nowadays, they did not sit all together as they had done in the past.

12
00:00:54,319 --> 00:01:00,279
Napoleon, with Squealer and another pig named Minimus, who had a remarkable gift

13
00:01:00,279 --> 00:01:05,640
for composing songs and poems, sat on the front of the raised platform with

14
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:12,640
the nine young dogs forming a semicircle round them and the other the sitting behind.

15
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:17,920
The rest of the animals sat facing them in the main body of the barn.

16
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:23,359
Napoleon read out the orders for the week in a gruff, soldierly style, and

17
00:01:23,359 --> 00:01:30,000
after a single singing of Beasts of England, all the animals dispersed.

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,479
On the third Sunday after Snowball's expulsion, the animals were somewhat

19
00:01:34,479 --> 00:01:40,159
surprised to hear Napoleon announce that the windmill was to be built after all.

20
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:44,239
He did not give any reason for having changed his mind, but merely warned the

21
00:01:44,239 --> 00:01:49,359
animals that this extra task would mean very hard work.

22
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:53,359
It might even be necessary to reduce their rations.

23
00:01:53,359 --> 00:01:58,600
The plans, however, had all been prepared down to the last detail.

24
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:04,359
A special committee of pigs had been at work upon them for the past 3 weeks.

25
00:02:04,359 --> 00:02:11,159
The building of the windmill, with various other improvements, was expected to take 2 years.

26
00:02:11,159 --> 00:02:15,239
That evening, Squealer explained privately to the other animals that

27
00:02:15,239 --> 00:02:19,760
Napoleon had never in reality been opposed to the windmill.

28
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:24,319
On the contrary, it was he who had advocated it in the beginning,

29
00:02:24,319 --> 00:02:28,279
and the plan which Snowball had drawn on the floor of the incubator shed had

30
00:02:28,279 --> 00:02:32,439
actually been stolen from among Napoleon's papers.

31
00:02:32,439 --> 00:02:38,439
The windmill was, in fact, Napoleon's own creation.

32
00:02:38,439 --> 00:02:40,800
"Why then?" asked somebody.

33
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:44,520
"Had he spoken so strongly against it?"

34
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:48,479
Here, Squealer looked very sly.

35
00:02:48,479 --> 00:02:53,279
"That," he said, "was Comrade Napoleon's cunning.

36
00:02:53,279 --> 00:02:57,640
He had seemed to oppose the windmill simply as a maneuver to get rid of

37
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:03,039
Snowball, who was a dangerous character and a bad influence.

38
00:03:03,039 --> 00:03:09,039
Now that Snowball was out of the way, the plan could go forward without his interference.

39
00:03:09,039 --> 00:03:14,760
This, said Squealer, was something called tactics.

40
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:20,399
He repeated a number of times, "Tactics, comrades, tactics!"

41
00:03:20,399 --> 00:03:24,520
skipping round and whisking his tail with a merry laugh.

42
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:28,600
The animals were not certain what the word meant, but Squealer spoke so

43
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,000
persuasively, and the three dogs who
